<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Cilicia</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 401 BCE (approx.) · capital Tarsus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Cilicia, a vassal kingdom of the Syennesis dynasty at Tarsus that kept its own kings under Persia until 401 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>, local rulers in the Cilician plain and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hilakku">Rough Cilicia</a> formed a kingdom with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarsus">Tarsus</a> as its capital, drawing on the lands of Que and Hilakku. Babylonian records call part of it Pirindu, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neriglissar">Neriglissar</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a> fought its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appuashu">Appuashu</a> in 557 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings bore the title or name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syennesis">Syennesis</a>. One Syennesis mediated, with a Babylonian envoy, the peace between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-lydia">Lydia</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/median-empire">Median Empire</a> after the eclipse battle of 585 BCE. Under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> the kingdom kept its own rulers, paid tribute in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and white horses and supplied ships to the Persian fleet.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 401 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syennesis">Syennesis</a> and his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epyaxa">Epyaxa</a> supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-younger">Cyrus the Younger</a> in his revolt. After its failure the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> abolished the kingship and turned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> into an ordinary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapy</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-cilicia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Cilicia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Rubenid_Dynasty.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 401 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tarsus</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Appuashu, Syennesis</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Luwian and Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Luwian, Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pirindu, Syennesid Cilicia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-500&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cilicia" aria-label="Kingdom of Cilicia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5555 848 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Cilicia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5875 1104L6140 1251"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6140 1251h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5875 1104h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5875 1104h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tarsus. <a href="/atlas?year=-500&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cilicia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
